{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"code-weight-one-type-dispatch-for-hashing-and-equality","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code weight: one type dispatch for hashing and equality"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reviewed executable revision: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"3b8412f4"},{"type":"text","value":" (base "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0122da80"},{"type":"text","value":", the fetched\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"origin/main"},{"type":"text","value":" at review time). This record follows in a documentation-only\ncommit. Work started on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"8283f2e8"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"f4c390a6"},{"type":"text","value":" merges "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0122da80"},{"type":"text","value":", which does\nnot change "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/db-ivm"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"c0182397"},{"type":"text","value":" adds the hash identity oracle and the work-cap tests on unchanged\nproduction code."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"d1fa5a9a"},{"type":"text","value":" is the refactor."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"b7455952"},{"type":"text","value":" extends the oracle after mutants on the refactor found three\ngrammar gaps."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"6073cb13"},{"type":"text","value":" applies review fixes. It fixes one performance regression and\none behavior change, and it closes three more grammar gaps."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"33603a2f"},{"type":"text","value":" compares type markers by object identity, after an external\nreview found that equality used random numbers as type identity."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"3b8412f4"},{"type":"text","value":" runs every oracle law in a module copy whose type markers all\ncollide, generates any value as a Map key, and aims half of the mutations\nat container nodes."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each version of the new tests also passes on the base code. The documentation\ncommit that follows also adds comments to the oracle file, with no executable\nchange."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"change","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Change"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hashObject"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"equalHashValues"},{"type":"text","value":" in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/db-ivm/src/hashing/hash.ts"},{"type":"text","value":"\neach had a six-way type dispatch: Date, binary, Temporal, RegExp, and the\nMap/Set/array/object shapes. Each branch had its own hasher or its own\ncomparison. One "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"objectParts(input)"},{"type":"text","value":" function now returns a\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[marker, header, body?]"},{"type":"text","value":" view that both use. Each marker is a private object\nthat holds a random hash number. Hashing writes the number, and equality\ncompares the objects by identity."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Header"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Body"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"timestamp, or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"invalid"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"none"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"binary (at most 128 bytes)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the bytes as one string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"none"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Temporal"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"type tag, string form"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"none"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"RegExp"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"source, flags, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lastIndex"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the RegExp"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Map"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"none"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"its entries"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"none"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"its values"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"array"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"length"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the array"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"object"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"none"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the object"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Also removed:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the four per-type hashers ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hashDate"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hashUint8Array"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hashTemporal"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hashPlainObject"},{"type":"text","value":") and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structuralShape"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the duplicate root and nested paths in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getCachedHash"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the unreachable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"typeof"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"default:"},{"type":"text","value":" warning in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"updateHasher"},{"type":"text","value":". The switch\nalready covers all eight "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"typeof"},{"type":"text","value":" results."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"referenceValues"},{"type":"text","value":" moved into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isReferenceHashedObject"},{"type":"text","value":", which both functions\nalready call."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The change is intended to preserve behavior. Hash values change because the\nbinary header is now a string. Hash values were never stable: the markers are\nrandom for each process, and nothing persists them."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,"right","right","right"],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Entry"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Revision"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"min"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"gzip"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"brotli"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"full "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/db"},{"type":"text","value":" (db-ivm inlined)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0122da80"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"378,307"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"106,762"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"90,361"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"3b8412f4"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"377,379"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"106,527"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"90,141"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Δ"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−928"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−235"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−220"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"standalone "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/db-ivm"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0122da80"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"34,374"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"10,570"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"9,513"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"3b8412f4"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"33,452"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"10,347"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"9,353"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Δ"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−922"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−223"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−160"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All numbers come from an esbuild bundle of the public entry, minified."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-earlier-versions-changed-and-what-this-change-keeps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What earlier versions changed, and what this change keeps"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The audit prototype (ledger IVM-01) and the first port of it changed the\nbehaviors below. This change keeps each one as the base code had it:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Work cap."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The prototype wrote every header value directly to the\nhasher. Array lengths and RegExp fields then stopped counting toward\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MAX_STRUCTURAL_HASH_WORK"},{"type":"text","value":", so a 1,000,000-element array was accepted\ninstead of rejected. Now header values of a type that has a body go through\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"updateHasher"},{"type":"text","value":", as before. Date, binary, and Temporal headers still cost\nnothing."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pair memo."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The prototype entered the equality pair memo before it\ncompared headers. That allocated memo entries for every Date, binary, and\nTemporal pair, and binary equality took 2.3 times as long. The first port\nmoved the whole memo after "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"objectParts"},{"type":"text","value":", which copies Map and Set entries.\nEach revisit of a shared or cyclic Map then cost O(entries): 100 revisits\nof one pair made 200 entry copies instead of 2. Now the lookup comes before\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"objectParts"},{"type":"text","value":", and the insert comes after the markers and headers match,\nonly for types with a body. That is the base order."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Arrays from another realm."}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"instanceof Array"},{"type":"text","value":" is false for an array\nfrom another realm, so both versions give it the object marker. The base\nequality also compared lengths with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Array.isArray"},{"type":"text","value":". The prototype dropped\nthat check. This change keeps it."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Header comparison."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The first port compared headers with the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NaN"},{"type":"text","value":"\nrule, so a RegExp whose "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lastIndex"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NaN"},{"type":"text","value":" equaled its copy. The base\ncode compared RegExp fields with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"!=="},{"type":"text","value":". Headers now compare with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"==="},{"type":"text","value":", and\nthe header of an invalid Date is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"invalid"},{"type":"text","value":", so all invalid dates stay equal."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type identity."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The base code told types apart with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"instanceof"},{"type":"text","value":". The\nfirst port compared the random marker numbers, so two types whose numbers\ncollided compared equal, for example an empty Map and an empty Set. Map and\narray then also gave different results in each argument order. Markers are\nnow objects, compared by identity."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"why-a-new-owner","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why a new owner"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before this change, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"equalHashValues"},{"type":"text","value":" had no direct test. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"topKBatch"},{"type":"text","value":" uses it\nto cancel a retraction against its replacement, and only\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tests/operators/topk-batch-contract.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" reached it. The hash-values\nowner ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hash.property.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":") checks pairwise hash laws on flat values. It\nhas no model of equality, and it does not generate Temporal values, RegExp\nfields, holes, symbol keys, registered handles, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"File"},{"type":"text","value":", or Map/Set order."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The new owner,\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/db-ivm/tests/hash-identity-oracle.property.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":", checks both\nfunctions against one identity model."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"contract-path-and-limits","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contract, path, and limits"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Authority: the method comments in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/hashing/hash.ts"},{"type":"text","value":", and the behavior at\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"8283f2e8"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Primitives compare by value. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-0"},{"type":"text","value":" equals "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NaN"},{"type":"text","value":" equals "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NaN"},{"type":"text","value":", and a\nbigint differs from the equal number. Symbols compare by identity."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Functions, registered handles, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"File"},{"type":"text","value":" values, and binary values over 128\nbytes compare by identity."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dates compare by timestamp. All invalid dates are equal."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Binary values of at most 128 bytes compare by bytes. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Buffer"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Uint8Array"},{"type":"text","value":" do not differ."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Temporal values compare by type tag and string form."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Regular expressions compare by source, flags, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lastIndex"},{"type":"text","value":", and enumerable\nown properties. The fields compare with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"==="},{"type":"text","value":", so a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NaN"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lastIndex"},{"type":"text","value":" never\nequals itself."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Arrays compare by length and enumerable own properties. A hole differs from\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Maps and Sets compare by entries or values in insertion order. Other\nproperties on a Map or Set do not count."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Other objects compare by enumerable own string and symbol properties, in\nany order. The prototype and non-enumerable properties do not count."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The model is a canonical encoding of a value "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"spec"}]},{"type":"text","value":", which is plain data.\nIt never reads a production object. The driver builds both sides of a pair as\nfresh objects from their specs. A seed varies property order, prototypes\n("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Object.create(null)"},{"type":"text","value":", a class instance), hidden non-enumerable\nproperties, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Buffer"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Uint8Array"},{"type":"text","value":", extra Map/Set properties, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-0"},{"type":"text","value":" for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":",\nand sharing or copying of a repeated subtree. None of these changes the\nidentity."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every law also runs in a second copy of the module, loaded with a\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"captureHashSession"},{"type":"text","value":" tape whose initialization draws are all equal. Every\nrandom constant, including every type marker, then has the same number, in any\ndeclaration order. A pinned case checks that precondition. In that copy, only\nthe sampled distinct-hash control is skipped."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For each acyclic pair, the check asserts:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"equalHashValues"},{"type":"text","value":" in both argument orders equals the model verdict."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Equal identities have equal hashes."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Distinct identities have distinct hashes. This is a sampled control, because\na 32-bit hash can collide."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cyclic values are chains of arrays, Map values, Sets, or plain objects with a\nback edge to an ancestor. For each one, the check asserts that\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"equalHashValues"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts a second build of the same spec and rejects a build\nwhere one leaf holds a text that no pool value has. It also asserts that "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hash"},{"type":"text","value":" throws\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Cannot hash cyclic structural values"},{"type":"text","value":". These verdicts come from\nconstruction, so the model needs no bisimulation rule."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hash-work.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" pins seven work-cap boundaries. Each case names the\nlargest input that fits, and the next size must throw. One more law counts Map\nentry copies: equality on 100 revisits of one shared Map pair copies entries\ntwice, once for each side."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Limits:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Arrays from another realm are outside the grammar. One pinned case holds\nequality's length check. Hashing gives such an array the object marker, so\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[1, <hole>]"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[1]"},{"type":"text","value":" from another realm hash equal but compare unequal.\nThis mismatch is present on the base revision too."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Map and Set order sensitivity, and ignored Map/Set properties, are pinned\ncurrent behavior. No contract promises them."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Getters and proxies are outside the grammar."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A RegExp with a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NaN"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lastIndex"},{"type":"text","value":" is outside the grammar. One pinned case\nholds strict comparison. Hashing normalizes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NaN"},{"type":"text","value":", so that pair hashes equal\nbut compares unequal. This mismatch is present on the base revision too."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cycles through a RegExp property, a Map key, or a symbol-keyed property are\noutside the grammar. So are pairs that differ only in where a back edge\npoints, such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"a = [a]"},{"type":"text","value":" against "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"b = [[b]]"},{"type":"text","value":". Those need a bisimulation\nmodel."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hash"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"equalHashValues"},{"type":"text","value":" still list enumerable own keys in two ways\n("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Object.keys"},{"type":"text","value":" plus symbols, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Reflect.ownKeys"},{"type":"text","value":"). The oracle's hidden\nnon-enumerable properties catch drift between them: mutant N16 fails."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Real Temporal types print distinct formats. Only a polyfill-shaped value can\nshare text across types, so one pinned case holds the type tag."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"grammar-controls-and-calibration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grammar controls and calibration"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Specs cover every kind in the contract, nested to a small depth. Map keys are\nany generated value. The model merges primitive keys and shared references\nthat are equal under SameValueZero, as Map and Set do: the first position\nstays and the last value wins. A pair is either the same spec (30%) or the\nspec with one near-miss mutation. Half of the mutations target a container\nnode, because leaves outnumber containers:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutation"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"header"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a Date timestamp, one binary byte, an appended byte, a Temporal value, RegExp flags or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lastIndex"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"hole"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"an appended hole, a hole for a value, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":" for a hole"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"order"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"reversed Map entries, Set values, or object keys (object order keeps the identity)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"property"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a renamed object or Map key, a repeated primitive Map key, a changed symbol key, an added RegExp or array property"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"retype"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A Date becomes its timestamp. Binary becomes an array of its bytes. A Map becomes a Set or an array of entry pairs. A Set becomes an array. An array becomes an object."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"replace"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a different primitive or reference id"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"split"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a shared child becomes two copies, one of them changed"}]}]]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reconstruction:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" 22 pinned pairs hold one rule each, in both module\ncopies. Six more pinned cases hold the Temporal tag, strict RegExp field\ncomparison, a shared child against two different copies, the cross-realm\nlength check, the colliding-marker precondition, and a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"topKBatch"},{"type":"text","value":"\nMap-to-Set replacement with colliding markers. One case builds the same\nshared/copied spec with 39 seed pairs."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ablation and exclusion:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the mutants below."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Range:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the positive execution witness requires the fixed campaign\n(seed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"2026930"},{"type":"text","value":", 300 pairs) to reach all 20 value kinds and all eight\nmutation classes, to give a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" verdict for header, hole, retype,\nreplace, and split mutations, and to give only "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" for unmutated pairs.\nIt also requires Map keys that are numbers, symbols, references, and\ncontainers, and at least one merged Map key."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each run executes a fixed campaign and a random campaign of 300 pairs for\nacyclic values, and the same for cyclic values.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TANSTACK_DB_IVM_HASH_IDENTITY_SEED"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TANSTACK_DB_IVM_HASH_IDENTITY_PATH"},{"type":"text","value":"\nselect a direct replay."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"source-mutants-on-unchanged-production-8283f2e8-sources","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source mutants on unchanged production ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"8283f2e8"},{"type":"text","value":" sources)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All rows use the tests at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"3b8412f4"},{"type":"text","value":". The columns count failures:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Identity oracle:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hash-identity-oracle.property.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" (34 cases)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Work-cap pins:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the seven boundary cases in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hash-work.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pre-existing:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" every other db-ivm test, with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hash-work.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" at its\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"origin/main"},{"type":"text","value":" version (589 tests)."}]}]}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutant"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Identity oracle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Work-cap pins"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pre-existing"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"W1: equality ignores RegExp "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lastIndex"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"assertion failure (3)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"0"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"ty